SunAlmanac (Garmin ConnectIQ) Widget
====================================
Almanac data and computations


Earth path around the Sun and its rotation upon itself are affected by external
parameters, such as the other planets position or the state of the inner core
magma.

Computing accurate sun events time requires to take those parameters into account,
based on the observations from the likes of the International Earth Rotation and
Reference Systems Service (IERS; https://www.iers.org), which are regularly updated.

Delta-T (TT-UT1)
----------------

The first step is to obtain the difference between the Terrestrial Time (TT)
and the Universal Time (UT1), as the value commonly referred to as Delta-T.

REFs:
 - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrestrial_Time
 - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_Time

Historically, this value could be obtained from the The US Naval Observatory's
Rapid Service/Prediction Center website (http://maia.usno.navy.mil), which is
nowadays no longer available.

REFs:
 - https://www.usno.navy.mil/USNO/earth-orientation/eo-products
 - http://maia.usno.navy.mil/ser7/deltat.preds

As of today, this value and its predictions may be obtained from the US Naval
Meteorology and Oceanography Command (https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil).

REFs:
 - https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil/Organization/United-States-Naval-Observatory/Earth-Orientation-Department/USNO-Earth-Orientation-Products/Long-term-Delta-T
 - https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil/Portals/49/deltat_data.txt   # example given
 - https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil/Portals/49/deltat_preds.txt  # example given


DUT1 (UT1-UTC)
--------------

Then, the difference between the Universal Time (UT) and the Coordinated
Universal Time (UTC), as the value commonly referred to as DUT1.

REFs:
 - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_Time
 - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coordinated_Universal_Time

Historically again, this value could be obtained from the The US Naval
Observatory's Rapid Service/Prediction Center website
(http://maia.usno.navy.mil).

REFs:
 - https://www.usno.navy.mil/USNO/earth-orientation/eo-products
 - http://maia.usno.navy.mil/ser7/ser7.dat

As of today, this value and its prediction formula may be obtained from the
International Earth Rotation and Reference Systems Service
(IERS; https://www.iers.org).

REFs:
 - https://www.iers.org/IERS/EN/Publications/Bulletins/bulletins.html
 - https://datacenter.iers.org/data/6/bulletina-xxxiv-049.txt  # example given


Julian Date
-----------

Most of those data are given relative to the Julian Date (JD) or Modified Julian Date (MJD),
which must be computed, relatively to the usual Gregorian calendar, by taking into account
such things as leap years and the likes.

REFs:
 - https://quasar.as.utexas.edu/BillInfo/JulianDatesG.html
 - https://core2.gsfc.nasa.gov/time/
